 # Changelog
 
+## 0.2.1 (unreleased)
+
+Additive; defaults and existing exports are unchanged.
+
+- Sanitizer profiles for the hosts that kept their own (#395), all opt-in on `SanitizeOptions` and all off by default: `allowSvg` (fixed shape allowlist; no script, style, foreignObject, use, image, animation or anchor; paint attributes may only reference local `url(#id)`), `allowMedia` (`picture`, `source`, `video`, `audio`; no autoplay; `src` follows the image policy, `poster` and `srcset` are dropped), `allowMathMl` (the KaTeX set), and `allowStyleProperties` (keeps `style` but only the listed properties with plain values; no `url(`, `var(`, `expression`, `@`, backslash or comments). New exports `SHIKI_SANITIZE_POLICY`, `KATEX_SANITIZE_POLICY`, `SVG_SANITIZE_POLICY` and the pure `filterStyleDeclarations`.
+- `SanitizeOptions.beforeSanitize(root)` runs once on the parsed, unsanitized tree (an inert `template` fragment) before sanitizing, so a host can stamp source positions on the original elements and still get sanitized output. It cannot widen the policy and is ignored with no DOM (the no-DOM path still escapes everything).
+- `MarkdownComponents` gains `strong`, `emphasis`, `delete`, `break`, `image` (policy-resolved `src`), `thematicBreak`, `list` (`ordered`, `start`), `frontmatter`, `math` (`inline` flag) and `html` (default sanitizes; return a node to show it as inert text) (#631). New `renderInline(source, options)` renders a short fragment with no block wrapper (#631).
+- `styles.css`: every `CodeBlock` colour (background, border, bar text, copy-button hover, copied and failed states, scrollbar) is a `var(--rk-...)` with the previous value as the fallback, so the block follows the app theme (#633). Document colours use the same tokens.
+- Not shipped: `form`, `base`, `meta`, `link`, `canvas` and `<style>` stay forbidden (a form can exfiltrate, `<style>` can restyle and overlay the host UI). A host that needs its own `base` or `meta` adds them after sanitizing. Not built or run locally; CI is the compiler.
+
 ## 0.2.0 (2026-10-17)
 
 - Sanitizer policy hooks (#395): `safeLinkHref(href, { allowTel, allowRelative })` and `sanitizeHtml`/`sanitizeMarkdownHtml(html, { allowTel, allowRelative, resolveImageSrc })`. Both link additions default off; tag, attribute and CSS allowlists are unchanged, and `javascript:`, `data:`, `srcdoc`, event handlers and styles stay refused. `resolveImageSrc` runs on relative image sources only; its return value is host-trusted.
